    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2c249d5e_aa3886ee",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/cros_flash/cros_flash_em32f967.c",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 273,
      "author": {
        "id": 1177449
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-29T08:12:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree that looping page‑erase logic conceptually belongs in the\nZephyr flash driver. For this change, it’s kept in the cros_flash layer\nto avoid refactoring the underlying flash driver, since the focus here\nis protection semantics rather than erase mechanics.",
      "parentUuid": "3f382606_ff546f2d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 262,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 273,
        "endChar": 2
      },
      "revId": "7e0310b07d1dd864f7ce27b01fcde2a28fd6109f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6b529adc_78df77b0",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/cros_flash/cros_flash_em32f967_wp.h",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 26,
      "author": {
        "id": 1441652
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-24T18:46:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is the protection range-based or sector-based? I guess your flash protection is range-based.\n\nI would not emulate the other type of protection mechanism. Mixing both in one driver causes confusion.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 26,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 26,
        "endChar": 53
      },
      "revId": "7e0310b07d1dd864f7ce27b01fcde2a28fd6109f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "33441e10_2c8c4153",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/cros_flash/cros_flash_em32f967_wp.h",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 26,
      "author": {
        "id": 1177449
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-29T08:12:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The protection mechanism is strictly range‑based.\n\nOn EM32F967, flash protection is configured only via contiguous protection\nranges using Protect Area registers. There is no sector‑ or bank‑level\nprotection configuration in hardware.\n\nThe `flash_em32_check_bank_protected()` helper does not introduce or emulate\na separate sector‑based protection mechanism. It simply answers whether a\ngiven bank falls within the currently configured protection range, as EC\nflash APIs are bank‑oriented for state reporting and policy decisions.\n\nSo the driver uses a single range‑based protection model, with bank‑based\nqueries only as a representation layer, not as a separate protection type.",
      "parentUuid": "6b529adc_78df77b0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 26,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 26,
        "endChar": 53
      },
